course: dictionary
lesson: 8780
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word shake has several meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. «Toad shakes his head and keeps on rowing.» Here shake means moving the head side to side to say no, because Toad is refusing to stop.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Shake hands» means to hold someone's hand and move it up and down to greet them. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit here? If it does not, try another meaning.
explain: Shake can also be a noun, a thing you can order. «I ordered a chocolate shake after school.» The word a in front and the drink in the sentence tell you a shake is something to drink, not a movement.
fact: Shake means to move something quickly up and down or side to side.
fact: To shake hands is to hold someone's hand and move it up and down to greet them.
fact: To shake can also mean to tremble, like shaking with cold or fear.
fact: A shake is a cold drink made with milk and ice cream.
fact: «In two shakes» means very soon, and «shake off» means get rid of.
exercise: «Toad shakes his head and keeps on rowing.» What does shake his head mean? | To wash it in the river | To rest it on his arms | To nod it up and down to say yes | *To move it side to side to say no
exercise: What does «shake hands» mean? | To wave goodbye from far away | *To hold someone's hand and move it up and down to greet them | To clap loudly at a show | To hide your hands in your pockets
exercise: «I ordered a chocolate shake after school.» What is a shake here? | A loud noise in the kitchen | *A cold drink made with milk and ice cream | A sudden movement of the ground | A type of handshake
test: «If you have a cold, you explain and wave instead of shaking hands.» Why do you wave instead? | Because your hands are too tired to move | Because waving is faster | Because shaking hands is always rude | *Because germs spread through hands
test: «Nerves can make even good voices shake.» What does shake mean here? | To mix up a drink | *To tremble or wobble | To move up and down to greet someone | To say no with your head
exam: How many handshakes happen when 4 children each shake hands once with every other child? | *6 | 4 | 8 | 12
